{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/585138-dark-eras-mage-selling-soul-to-the-devil","id":585138,"title":"[Dark Eras Mage] Selling soul to the Devil","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-09T13:57:56-07:00","id":585138,"title":"[Dark Eras Mage] Selling soul to the Devil","content":"I watched today Tim Burton's <b><i>Sleepy Hallow</i></b> and I remebered old tradition of witchcraft - selling soul to the Satan. Adversary. The Devil. As system, <b>Mage </b>use this tradition in the ways of Mastigos Path, but as the whole, it's based more on idea of Supernal World of something great, powerfull and &quot;good&quot; for the life of sorcerer. There is disonance between real world occult practice and game as based on those.<br /> <br /> Looking in times between late antiquity and modern era ( like between III to XIX century, highest in &quot;Witch Trails&quot; Eras ) we see in occult lore that witches are &quot;commuting with Devil&quot; on they own, free will. They dwell in to negative symbols to overthrow rigid strutures of society that do not understand they point of view. They sell they life to work for the dark forces - at least what they percive them. And surely all of them would not be Mastigos only - &quot;witch&quot; is official title for Acanthus Path now, don't they? From XIX century we see more &quot;scientific&quot; way approches to Mysteries, to contacting the dead, spiritual plane or just higher realms. But before - the sorcerers were going to get last Everlasting Damnation only for the power to bend the Fallen World under their fingertips.<br /> <br /> <b>So <i>who</i> sell the souls to the Devil in <i>Dark Eras</i> of Mage? <i>Why</i> they do it? And who is <i>the Devil</i> they go on pact with to damn their Soul from the light of Heaven?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-09-2015, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T14:12:02-07:00","id":585181,"title":"","content":"They probably don't. To the extent that they affect the Awakened, witch trials seem to be cover for Banishers and Seers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T14:23:16-07:00","id":585196,"title":"","content":"The closest you'll get sound like the Antimonian practices that Mages sometimes employ. They deliberately shun or invert normal societal values in order to determine their true value and for the power of being the kind of person who can and will do the unexpected or seemingly impossible.<br /> <br /> Anyways, just signing your name to a Watchtower is a metaphor for selling your soul, so work with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T14:30:31-07:00","id":585202,"title":"","content":"Thinking more about it, very powerfull Beast, Shade, Fae or Demon can be seen as Satan-like being to those that do not studied Occult before their Awakening...<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Exarchs can be seen as the Devil - they want to brought missery on all human kind, only for your payment in powers. Does this mean the pre-modern witches were mostly Seers of Throne? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-09-2015, 05:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T14:40:41-07:00","id":585233,"title":"","content":"Summoners has a whole pact system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T14:41:07-07:00","id":585235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/585138-dark-eras-mage-selling-soul-to-the-devil?p=585202#post585202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking more about it, very powerfull Beast, Shade, Fae or Demon can be seen as Satan-like being to those that do not studied Occult before their Awakening...<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Exarchs can be seen as the Devil - they want to brought missery on all human kind, only for your payment in powers. Does this mean the pre-modern witches were mostly Seers of Throne? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, it doesn't. Also you don't need to bring in supernatural stuff from other game lines just to get a &quot;Sold my soul&quot; vibe. <br /> <br /> Mastigos see devils in the Supernal, they're the classic example of someone who sells their soul for power. I actually played a Mastigos who literally believed he had sold his soul in order to Awaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T15:52:27-07:00","id":585305,"title":"","content":"How about Inferno? I haven't had a chance to read it cover-to-cover, but I think there might be something there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T16:01:42-07:00","id":585308,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't this just be Scelesti of the era? Selling their souls to Abyssal &quot;demons&quot; that they give shape to by twisting the mainstream christians and their faith, considering the annunaki as greater archdemons, and perhaps give the whole abyss a singular manifestation as Satan. Itd make sense--much like the colonists of Salem mustve all felt, it was a lonely, scary world for everyone, even a witch. Much as the puritans took comfort in imagining Jesus was with them and their hard works served both community and God, so too might the Infernalists take comfort in believing their Dark Friend was out in the terrifying woods, controlling everything chaotic and &quot;outside&quot;, giving meaning to the rejection of society by the witch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":935,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","user":"Cleverest of Things","date":". 07-09-2015, 07:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T17:12:02-07:00","id":585394,"title":"","content":"It wouldn't be just the Scelesti, but that's a cool take on one possibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T17:58:42-07:00","id":585487,"title":"","content":"It would be interesting if they had their own societ, a mix of Inferno, Scelesti, Liches, heretics. Couldve rivaled the pentacle in the new world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T21:29:28-07:00","id":585633,"title":"","content":"Okay, so in the order of showing up in the topic... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/585138-dark-eras-mage-selling-soul-to-the-devil?p=585235#post585235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it doesn't. Also you don't need to bring in supernatural stuff from other game lines just to get a &quot;Sold my soul&quot; vibe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beasts, Demons, Fae and Shades are all the stuff from Mage - they are Supernal Enteties from, resepctively, Primal Wild, Pandemonium, Arcadia and Stygia. Mages often see them in their Awakening an later, if they use 2ED Mage Sight. I only missed Angels of Aether, beacuse - well - they are Angels, most Monotheistic-raised Awakened just assume that &quot;God have chosen them&quot;, not that they &quot;sold their soul to the Devil&quot;.<br /> <br /> So ya, you are partially right - Antimonia would be very often practice of the Paths that do not work with Christianity cosmology ( i.e. every other beside the Obrimos ). Those self-taughted mages raised as Christian, but seeing other Realms that Aether, need to reconsider they views and often, they think their joined with Devil.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/585138-dark-eras-mage-selling-soul-to-the-devil?p=585235#post585235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mastigos see devils in the Supernal, they're the classic example of someone who sells their soul for power. I actually played a Mastigos who literally believed he had sold his soul in order to Awaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>But not all characters like this would be Mastigos. In Witch Trials Era, any non-Obrimos sorceres can be called &quot;witch&quot; becuase they pracie are mostly &quot;heretical&quot; or &quot;pagan&quot; - and in reality just not working with Christian paradigm.<br /> <br /> Example is in the Sleepy Hallow movie. It's spoiler, so I mark it in here - read on your own mind.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Headless Raider is clearly controlled by the Moros mage. Character is not &quot;devious&quot;, rather is &quot;morderous&quot; and dedivated to death and wealth.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I wanted to broaden the presepctive beside the Mastigos Path on the topic here, because it's easy asnwer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/585138-dark-eras-mage-selling-soul-to-the-devil?p=585305#post585305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about Inferno? I haven't had a chance to read it cover-to-cover, but I think there might be something there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, Inferno would work - only, it's just limited view. But for the Apostates that summon Inferno demons, it clearly works.<br /> <br /> Mostly, I strive to analyze core <b>Mage</b> setting, so make it easy to use in Dark Eras - and maybe from time to time in moden. Like in <a href=\"http://www.dailymail.co.uk/news/article-3144213/ISIS-executes-women-beheading-time-group-kills-two-married-couples-witchcraft-sorcery-Syria.html\" target=\"_blank\">Syria ISIS is witch hunting women &quot;for magic&quot;</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/585138-dark-eras-mage-selling-soul-to-the-devil?p=585308#post585308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't this just be Scelesti of the era? Selling their souls to Abyssal &quot;demons&quot; that they give shape to by twisting the mainstream christians and their faith, considering the annunaki as greater archdemons, and perhaps give the whole abyss a singular manifestation as Satan. Itd make sense--much like the colonists of Salem mustve all felt, it was a lonely, scary world for everyone, even a witch. Much as the puritans took comfort in imagining Jesus was with them and their hard works served both community and God, so too might the Infernalists take comfort in believing their Dark Friend was out in the terrifying woods, controlling everything chaotic and &quot;outside&quot;, giving meaning to the rejection of society by the witch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seclasti are also easy answer - those that are left alone go for the Dark Arts to servivie on alone, without cabals. And I still thinks that Exarchs could work as Devil Figurein here, beside Abyss and a like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/585138-dark-eras-mage-selling-soul-to-the-devil?p=585487#post585487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be interesting if they had their own societ, a mix of Inferno, Scelesti, Liches, heretics. Couldve rivaled the pentacle in the new world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have other idea - what if the Pentacle is not strong in the world at large? What if the Witch Trials decimiated the population of mages and only very big cities have Consillia still? Then lone Awakened, practing Left-Hand arts ( then called Nephandi ) would be much more prominent. Like the saying say: &quot;When the cat's away the mice will play&quot;. Or in our example - &quot;When Consillium away the Nephandi play&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> This and need for Antimonia even in normal Awakened becuase of oppresing teachings of Christanity in most of Old and New World - and you have easily the source for mages trying to use Dark Arts just to oppose the Witch Hunters on their trail, thinking they sold their souls to Devil.<br /> <br /> Is this working? What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-10-2015, 12:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T21:49:02-07:00","id":585647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/585138-dark-eras-mage-selling-soul-to-the-devil?p=585633#post585633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I only missed Angels of Aether, beacuse - well - they are Angels, most Monotheistic-raised Awakened just assume that &quot;God have chosen them&quot;, not that they &quot;sold their soul to the Devil&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lucifer was an angel as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In Witch Trials Era, any non-Obrimos sorceres can be called &quot;witch&quot; becuase they pracie are mostly &quot;heretical&quot; or &quot;pagan&quot; - and in reality just not working with Christian paradigm. </div> </div> </div>There's a somewhat famous historical instance of the Catholic Church having to tamp down on the practice of praying to angels and the various Protestant faiths don't really have much to do with the Heavenly Host by comparison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T00:31:03-07:00","id":585726,"title":"","content":"Hamster, one thing about devilry: it's all either in accusations or confessions under torture, which - contrary to what <i>24</i> etc. tells you - will only get you what the torturer wants to hear, in this case deals with the devil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T02:00:22-07:00","id":585777,"title":"","content":"Ah, I assumed you were bringing in other supernatural groups for some reason, my bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T02:17:09-07:00","id":585783,"title":"","content":"I've been mulling over the idea of a Christian Great Cult in the style of To The Strongest. I mean, Christianity is such an integral part of peoples world views it's seems not implausible you'd have something like a great cult reappearing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But not all characters like this would be Mastigos. In Witch Trials Era, any non-Obrimos sorceres can be called &quot;witch&quot; becuase they pracie are mostly &quot;heretical&quot; or &quot;pagan&quot; - and in reality just not working with Christian paradigm. </div> </div> </div>That's not exactly true. There are plenty of real people who thought/claimed they could do magic. Using celestial spirits or 'natural magic' went along fine with a Christian understanding of the universe. Even demon summoning is somewhat justifiable by the legends of King Solomon. The Mastigos path is actually riffing on that legend far more than the idea of signing your soul over to the devil. The righteous man whose wisdom allows him to command demons.<br /> <br /> The thing to remember is that witch trials only really work if the 'witch' is a person of comparatively normal social status. You don't accuse gentry of being in league with satan (or if you do, you do it in private). In reality, the people actually practicing magic were people of fairly high status. You need to be quite well educated before you can start reading magic texts afterall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T02:57:19-07:00","id":585808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/585138-dark-eras-mage-selling-soul-to-the-devil?p=585783#post585783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been mulling over the idea of a Christian Great Cult in the style of To The Strongest. I mean, Christianity is such an integral part of peoples world views it's seems not implausible you'd have something like a great cult reappearing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would gladly see that! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/585138-dark-eras-mage-selling-soul-to-the-devil?p=585783#post585783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not exactly true. There are plenty of real people who thought/claimed they could do magic. Using celestial spirits or 'natural magic' went along fine with a Christian understanding of the universe. Even demon summoning is somewhat justifiable by the legends of King Solomon. The Mastigos path is actually riffing on that legend far more than the idea of signing your soul over to the devil. The righteous man whose wisdom allows him to command demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>But AWAKENING to the Primal Wild, Stygia, Pandemonium or Arcadia cannot be reconsider with Christians view on &quot;godly actions&quot;. Those that would Awaken on those Paths will see themselves more like at least sinners, if not full pagan in Christian-ruled society of Middle Ages and early Modern Era.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/585138-dark-eras-mage-selling-soul-to-the-devil?p=585783#post585783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing to remember is that witch trials only really work if the 'witch' is a person of comparatively normal social status. You don't accuse gentry of being in league with satan (or if you do, you do it in private). In reality, the people actually practicing magic were people of fairly high status. You need to be quite well educated before you can start reading magic texts afterall.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, from when Awakening in <b>Mage </b>need you to be highly educated? Yes, reading texts and collecting knowledge is very helpful and is entire reason of Mysterium, but Awakening does not this things to break the Sleep in future mage. You can easily have &quot;hedge witches&quot; from Traditions followers or those joining to the Nameless Orders that will some day become Free Council, not Pentacle. I even assume that in New World Nameless are much more prevalent in early Modern Era ( From 1500 to 1800 ), steadily rising in power, to finally breaking in to Nameless War of XIX century.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T08:13:23-07:00","id":586108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/585138-dark-eras-mage-selling-soul-to-the-devil?p=585808#post585808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But AWAKENING to the Primal Wild, Stygia, Pandemonium or Arcadia cannot be reconsider with Christians view on &amp;quot;godly actions&amp;quot;. Those that would Awaken on those Paths will see themselves more like at least sinners, if not full pagan in Christian-ruled society of Middle Ages and early Modern Era.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is inaccurate. It's true that many who Awaken to those Paths might feel like outsiders to Christianity proper, but they would be just as likely to spin up some rationalization about their purpose in the faith as they would be to reject it or feel tainted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T10:47:46-07:00","id":586260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/585138-dark-eras-mage-selling-soul-to-the-devil?p=585808#post585808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, from when Awakening in <b>Mage </b>need you to be highly educated?</div> </div> </div> </div>He was saying that people in real life who thought/claimed they could do magic were educated people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T10:55:39-07:00","id":586265,"title":"","content":"Primal Wild or Arcadia= Garden of Eden<br /> <br /> Stygia= the Limbo<br /> <br /> Pandemonium= Purgatory<br /> <br /> There's indeed way to frame every Awakening in any religious worldview.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T14:59:00-07:00","id":586468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But AWAKENING to the Primal Wild, Stygia, Pandemonium or Arcadia cannot be reconsider with Christians view on &quot;godly actions&quot;. Those that would Awaken on those Paths will see themselves more like at least sinners, if not full pagan in Christian-ruled society of Middle Ages and early Modern Era. </div> </div> </div>This is kinda my point about the Great cult idea. I agree, it's not immediately obvious, but it's far from impossible with a bit of work. We already have awakened Kabbalah which was popular around the same time as witch trials.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wait, from when Awakening in <b>Mage </b>need you to be highly educated? </div> </div> </div>As Kazorh said, I'm making a point about the people who in history actually practiced magic. My point is that historically, it was extremely easy to get away with being a magician as long as you could actually back that power up (in real life by being of high status, and with the Awakened, having actual magic).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T15:06:01-07:00","id":586469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/585138-dark-eras-mage-selling-soul-to-the-devil?p=586265#post586265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Primal Wild or Arcadia= Garden of Eden</div> </div> </div> </div>Garden of Eden with few meters tall monsterous Beasts hunting on you? Sounds not very Bible-like...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/585138-dark-eras-mage-selling-soul-to-the-devil?p=586265#post586265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stygia= the Limbo<br /> <br /> Pandemonium= Purgatory</div> </div> </div> </div>Does not sining yourself to Limbo or even Hell ( Pandemonium looks much more like classical Hell to Christians than Purgaotry ) did not would made Christian to think he's doomed his soul from the Heaven's Ethernal Light?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/585138-dark-eras-mage-selling-soul-to-the-devil?p=586265#post586265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's indeed way to frame every Awakening in any religious worldview.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tower of Babel could work as nice Atlantis Fall metaphor, but we still have Awakenings that basiclyy say to Chrisitan &quot;You will not go to Heaven for Rest Ethernal&quot;...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T15:10:01-07:00","id":586470,"title":"","content":"Yeah, if you're determined to make it not work. It's not going to work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T15:11:15-07:00","id":586472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/585138-dark-eras-mage-selling-soul-to-the-devil?p=586469#post586469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Garden of Eden with few meters tall monsterous Beasts hunting on you? Sounds not very Bible-like...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno about that...<br /> <br /> Genesis 2:19<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Now the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Lord</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> God had formed out of the ground all the wild animals</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> and all the birds in the sky.</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> He brought them to the man to see what he would name them; and whatever the man called</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> each living creature,</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> that was its name.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Considering every creature that has ever existed on Earth? I'd say some of them would be pretty monstrous seeming. Especially if you include the supernatural stuff in nWoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T16:17:18-07:00","id":586530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/585138-dark-eras-mage-selling-soul-to-the-devil?p=586469#post586469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Garden of Eden with few meters tall monsterous Beasts hunting on you? Sounds not very Bible-like...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Does not sining yourself to Limbo or even Hell ( Pandemonium looks much more like classical Hell to Christians than Purgaotry ) did not would made Christian to think he's doomed his soul from the Heaven's Ethernal Light?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Tower of Babel could work as nice Atlantis Fall metaphor, but we still have Awakenings that basiclyy say to Chrisitan &quot;You will not go to Heaven for Rest Ethernal&quot;...</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, there's a whole vampire group that works itself into Christian mythology despite being blood suckers. Signing to Pandemonium is not a problem for staying Christian.<br /> <br /> Or to take it back to Mage, the Concordat of the Serpent models itself after the mythology of the serpent from the Garden of Eden. Nowhere in their write up does it say that they feel rejected by God, despite that being the explicit fate of the serpent in the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 07-10-2015, 07:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T23:33:11-07:00","id":586851,"title":"","content":"I've thought for a while that a Left-Handed Legacy based on Inferno Pacts would be a strong antagonist sect.<br /> <br /> I think Second Edition should release a larger scale &quot;Inferno&quot; book that serves to reintroduce not just material from the first book, but also Belial's Brood, the Bale Hounds, and other such groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T02:23:39-07:00","id":586927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/585138-dark-eras-mage-selling-soul-to-the-devil?p=586851#post586851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've thought for a while that a Left-Handed Legacy based on Inferno Pacts would be a strong antagonist sect.<br /> <br /> I think Second Edition should release a larger scale &quot;Inferno&quot; book that serves to reintroduce not just material from the first book, but also Belial's Brood, the Bale Hounds, and other such groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Agree. We need an infernalist faction for every major super. I think Changelings are going to be the scariest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T07:31:33-07:00","id":587079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've thought for a while that a Left-Handed Legacy based on Inferno Pacts would be a strong antagonist sect.</div> </div> </div> </div> How's that? <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Second Edition should release a larger scale &quot;Inferno&quot; book</div> </div> </div> </div> You mean the Second Edition of the World of Darkness in general, yes? <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">that serves to reintroduce not just material from the first book, but also Belial's Brood, the Bale Hounds, and other such groups.</div> </div> </div> </div> What other such groups? Every scary and barely related antagonist type from each of the gamelines? Aren't they better off just being in distinct books serving their own game lines?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T07:37:46-07:00","id":587111,"title":"","content":"I think for mages, if one is developing an idea of an individual or group with some kind of association with some demonic power, one has to consider what the motivation of the mage is in a manner that actually realtes to the cosmology of the game and how it affects the outlook of mages. It's like, you get a Seer of the Throne, and they serve the Exarchs because of their perspective on how the Supernal and the Fallen relate to one another and this idea that the only effective (or at least safe) way to approach Mysteries is through service to this preeminant thing in the Supernal. You have Scelesti, who can be fairly diverse, but still kind of ultimately revolve around an idea about what has shape and meaning in reality and how to seek forms of transcendence. You have Goetic Legacies based around harnessing demons for the sake of self-control and perfection... What does &quot;infernalism&quot; do that compares to any of that, that makes it actually fit coherently into the game? What makes it more than just rote and generic? What makes Vice-based demons something to serve, for people who already have magical powers, rather than just another Mystery to explore and exploit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T10:19:52-07:00","id":587231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/585138-dark-eras-mage-selling-soul-to-the-devil?p=587079#post587079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> How's that? You mean the Second Edition of the World of Darkness in general, yes? What other such groups? Every scary and barely related antagonist type from each of the gamelines? Aren't they better off just being in distinct books serving their own game lines?</div> </div> </div> </div>No other groups of Infernalists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T10:24:53-07:00","id":587236,"title":"","content":"Summoners deals with that sort of thing - mages selling their souls to various types of creatures. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T01:39:42-07:00","id":587951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">No other groups of Infernalists.</div> </div> </div> </div> Bale Hounds being associated with the Maeljin I'll grant, but I don't know if there's a connection to Belial's Brood and really don't think there should be. Overall, I feel as though an approach of &quot;these antagonists from Werewolf, Vampire, and Mage if we can come up with anything, or all actually intrusions of this one blue book supplement into all of their game lines&quot; is undesirable for several reasons, not least of which is that reducing those two lines' antagonists down to &quot;Infernalists&quot; seems like a step towards making them generic and uninteresting and not really fitting to their respective settings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T03:07:51-07:00","id":587992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/585138-dark-eras-mage-selling-soul-to-the-devil?p=587951#post587951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">not least of which is that reducing those two lines' antagonists down to &quot;Infernalists&quot; seems like a step towards making them generic and uninteresting and not really fitting to their respective settings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cuting Bale Hounds entirely for Werewolf 2ED corebook made them really not fitting in to their setting... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T12:44:08-07:00","id":588400,"title":"","content":"I understand that the rationale there was that there was not enough room to do them justice, which seems like rather the opposite of disavowing them. I recall that it is actually going to be similarly implemented for the Mage Second Edition core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T14:40:34-07:00","id":609973,"title":"","content":"Thinking more on last two weeks about subject of &quot;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deal_with_the_Devil\" target=\"_blank\">selling soul to Devil</a>&quot; and reading mine source on witch trials ( Polish <i>Focus Extra</i> about witches ) - <b>I think best is to leave it as general Awakening, in popular form signing the Watchtower with paper, book or even skin in Mystery Play to get a &quot;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chirograph\" target=\"_blank\">chierograph</a>&quot;. </b>In those Dark Eras using magic was consider Devil's work, whatever you personally thought about it.<br /> <br /> Question remains - <b>Who of Awakened would consider themselves to &quot;sell a soul&quot;</b> - Diamond mages, as allegory for Oracles? Sees of Throne, for working with Exarchs? Or maybe various Nameless that do not understand cosmology from their limited perspective? Maybe even Scelasti, but on the other hand they does not work with seeing Supernal = Devil kind of thing if they worship Abyss. <b>Who of Awakened would been <i>proud</i> of his act of &quot;selling soul&quot; to tell his enemies about it in open?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-31-2015, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T15:26:49-07:00","id":610030,"title":"","content":"Probably any of them given the right set of circumstances. It's not like Mages are known for being humble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T13:56:52-07:00","id":683529,"title":"","content":"Some film that could nicely work with topic idea of Left-Hand mages in <b>Dark Eras</b>...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kvRHjkxj0Xk\" data-code=\"kvRHjkxj0Xk\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/kvRHjkxj0Xk/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T18:18:51-07:00","id":685114,"title":"","content":"Why do you think Obrimos is not fit for the entire &quot;deal with the devil&quot; aspect? For starters, the term angels is just what mage society calls them. They have nothing to do with the biblical angels - unless you want them to.<br /> <br /> One picture of the aether is an entirely burning world, everything is in flames. This is as close to either the medieval image of hell, as you can get, or it can also be an image for judgement day, where the sinners are all burned.<br /> Angels by default don't look like winged humans in white. They can also look like dragons, gryphons, other mystical beasts assotiated with fire/energy/movement...<br /> With everything reflecting energy, forces and light, you get an image that could be very close to a biblical heaven (if you focus on the light parts), or hell (if you go for fire), or entirely unrelated to it, e.g. if you consider that whether is also a domain of the realm =&gt; storms and rain and lightning come to mind. Also: energy and forces can be quite destructive, regardless if they are vulcanos, earthquakes, explosions, nuclear bombs or evaporizing laser beams, etc....<br /> <br /> Combining any supernal realm with christian faith is just a question of coming up with the right ideas. Pandemonium can e.g. actually look like the the catacombs under Rome or old temple ruins, Stygia might have sanctified aspects of graveyards, or maybe there's a huge cathedral, where the souls of the dead are waiting for judgement day... the primal wild could be really biblical in the sense of the story of the creation of the world and then:&quot;And God blessed them. And God said to them, \u201cBe fruitful and multiply and fill the earth and subdue it, and have dominion over the fish of the sea and over the birds of the heavens and over every living thing that moves on the earth.\u201d (Gen 1.28). That doesn sound VERY primal wild to me: Procreate, hunt, conquer. If you look for beasts in the bible, the old testament has enough of them, right now I remember the story with Jonah and the wale. Arcadia is probably the most creative realm, and the fae might give you the clearest image of heaven - if they wish so. And that's just as likely as that they show you a torture chamber or a pagan ceremony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3278,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3278-tyloron","user":"Tyloron","date":". 10-01-2015, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3278-tyloron","name":"Tyloron","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T00:48:29-07:00","id":685340,"title":"","content":"In my experience Wyrd tends to be a very literal person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T04:41:28-07:00","id":959173,"title":"","content":"Watching 2<sup>nd</sup> season of <b>Penny Dreadful</b> ( especially episode 3 ) I got final inspiration to create truly witch sabbath Nameless Order. So here it is.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Nameless Order - Lovers of Devil</span></b><br /> For almost millennium, Church has accused many women and man of contacts with Devil and getting sorcery powers from this. Many Awakened were misunderstood because of it \u2013 to Christians what was Supernal has become Hell, spells became curses and High Speech of Atlantis was Devil\u2019s Tounge. Lovers of Devil are Nameless that embraced those accusations and worship Dark One as their patron. More, they really can summon things that anyone could only describe as demons from Hell.<br /> <br /> Awakened from Pentacle or Seers alike agree that Lovers have made in compact with some being from Lower Depths that want to spread sin and wickedness. Mysterium scholars call this dimension as Inferno, but any other can simply call it Hell. As now labeled as Left Hand practice, it lived for almost one thousand years on outskirts of Awakened communities. Most of new members were coming from Nameless that were left on their own \u2013 when they uncovered cursed Grimoire or relict of previous sabbath, Lovers come in compact with lower demons from this realm and form covens around it. Their patrons give them clues and advices to find other of their kind, forming loose alliance over whole countries or continents.<br /> <br /> <b>Order Tools:</b> Blood, sacrifice, orgies.<br /> <br /> <b>Initiation</b><br /> 1: Patron \u2013 Novice in coven need to make Pact with Patron of it, being able to communicate with Inferno demon by rituals.<br /> 2: High Speech ( as Devils Tongue )<br /> 3: Vice-Ridden ( CoD Rulebook )<br /> 4: Library (Occult) 3<br /> 5: Summoning \u2013 Highest witch in sabbath can summon it\u2019s Patron as instant action by connection it have with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T13:13:43-07:00","id":959398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/585138-dark-eras-mage-selling-soul-to-the-devil?p=959173#post959173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Watching 2<sup>nd</sup> season of <b>Penny Dreadful</b> ( especially episode 3 ) I got final inspiration to create truly witch sabbath Nameless Order. So here it is.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Nameless Order - Lovers of Devil</span></b><br /> For almost millennium, Church has accused many women and man of contacts with Devil and getting sorcery powers from this. Many Awakened were misunderstood because of it \u2013 to Christians what was Supernal has become Hell, spells became curses and High Speech of Atlantis was Devil\u2019s Tounge. Lovers of Devil are Nameless that embraced those accusations and worship Dark One as their patron. More, they really can summon things that anyone could only describe as demons from Hell.<br /> <br /> Awakened from Pentacle or Seers alike agree that Lovers have made in compact with some being from Lower Depths that want to spread sin and wickedness. Mysterium scholars call this dimension as Inferno, but any other can simply call it Hell. As now labeled as Left Hand practice, it lived for almost one thousand years on outskirts of Awakened communities. Most of new members were coming from Nameless that were left on their own \u2013 when they uncovered cursed Grimoire or relict of previous sabbath, Lovers come in compact with lower demons from this realm and form covens around it. Their patrons give them clues and advices to find other of their kind, forming loose alliance over whole countries or continents.<br /> <br /> <b>Order Tools:</b> Blood, sacrifice, orgies.<br /> <br /> <b>Initiation</b><br /> 1: Patron \u2013 Novice in coven need to make Pact with Patron of it, being able to communicate with Inferno demon by rituals.<br /> 2: High Speech ( as Devils Tongue )<br /> 3: Vice-Ridden ( CoD Rulebook )<br /> 4: Library (Occult) 3<br /> 5: Summoning \u2013 Highest witch in sabbath can summon it\u2019s Patron as instant action by connection it have with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No sex with goats? I am disappointed! (looks good, actually).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12017-ehkesoyo","name":"Ehkesoyo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12017_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T17:50:02-07:00","id":959588,"title":"","content":"Just a minor note, but between the last line of the Patron tools section in the core and how they're used in the Sundered World setting, don't forget that you can offer Patron tool Yantras as a benefit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T23:05:36-07:00","id":959680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ehkesoyo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/585138-dark-eras-mage-selling-soul-to-the-devil?p=959398#post959398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No sex with goats? I am disappointed! (looks good, actually).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in the 'orgies' Tool. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/585138-dark-eras-mage-selling-soul-to-the-devil?p=959588#post959588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a minor note, but between the last line of the Patron tools section in the core and how they're used in the Sundered World setting, don't forget that you can offer Patron tool Yantras as a benefit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but still do not have idea how those would work here. Any thought on possible Patron Tools?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-09T16:13:36-07:00","id":1486124,"title":"","content":"Coming in late, but a comment made by local Changelings in one of my old games when learning of how Mages sign their names to Watchtowers brought forth the comment - &quot;So, you sold your <i>name</i> to this 'Watchtower'? Do you have any idea what kind of contract you've made?&quot; The local Changeling Motley shuddered in terror when they head about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-09T17:42:43-07:00","id":1486129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Armsley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/585138-dark-eras-mage-selling-soul-to-the-devil?p=1486124#post1486124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Coming in late, but a comment made by local Changelings in one of my old games when learning of how Mages sign their names to Watchtowers brought forth the comment - &quot;So, you sold your <i>name</i> to this 'Watchtower'? Do you have any idea what kind of contract you've made?&quot; The local Changeling Motley shuddered in terror when they head about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have centuries of research and data, so far the only ones who they can confirm sold themselves are the Prelates, most Seers are more like contract workers. They extensively verified this research using the knowledge database connected to said suspicious power source. Huh, maybe that wasn't the best idea...... but its on a dimension/layer of reality that you can't directly interact without being made deader than dead, so what options are there ?<br /> <br /> But they escaped the cage of the Lie, just like changelings escaped their Durance. Their Wyrd based powers give them a lot of insight into deals and contracts, it only gives them the rope to hang themselves, it doesn't put it around their necks, right ? Surely Awakened magic is the same, it has to be.......","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-10T12:07:31-07:00","id":1486169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Armsley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/585138-dark-eras-mage-selling-soul-to-the-devil?p=1486124#post1486124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Coming in late, but a comment made by local Changelings in one of my old games when learning of how Mages sign their names to Watchtowers brought forth the comment - &quot;So, you sold your <i>name</i> to this 'Watchtower'? Do you have any idea what kind of contract you've made?&quot; The local Changeling Motley shuddered in terror when they head about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose it's only fair to have at least one instance where it's the changelings erroneously assuming their cosmology's rules are in charge for mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T12:57:50-07:00","id":1490164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/585138-dark-eras-mage-selling-soul-to-the-devil?p=1486169#post1486169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose it's only fair to have at least one instance where it's the changelings erroneously assuming their cosmology's rules are in charge for mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>And vice versa. An NPC Thyrsus tried to Control Spirit on a gob, and that didn't work out well. Understanding non-Supernal stuff is a continuing research subject for the Mysterium in my Mage. But Mages are The Wise - an Acanthus who uses Fate and Prime sight can unravel what an active Contract is about, for example.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it's my personal headfanon that the Watchtowers *are* the Oracles, who made the ultimate sacrifice and performed the highest Imperial working possible to keep magic alive. They don't act because they are symbols of freedom that oppose the Exarchs, and coercion is literally antithetical to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T13:01:16-07:00","id":1490166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/585138-dark-eras-mage-selling-soul-to-the-devil?p=1486169#post1486169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose it's only fair to have at least one instance where it's the changelings erroneously assuming their cosmology's rules are in charge for mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, names are a big, big deal for Changelings. The Lost may be closer to the truth in thinking that the names for the Watchtowers are names of Keeper-like beings who contract with Mages.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T13:12:41-07:00","id":1490168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Armsley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/585138-dark-eras-mage-selling-soul-to-the-devil?p=1490164#post1490164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And vice versa. An NPC Thyrsus tried to Control Spirit on a gob, and that didn't work out well. Understanding non-Supernal stuff is a continuing research subject for the Mysterium in my Mage. But Mages are The Wise - an Acanthus who uses Fate and Prime sight can unravel what an active Contract is about, for example.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it's my personal headfanon that the Watchtowers *are* the Oracles, who made the ultimate sacrifice and performed the highest Imperial working possible to keep magic alive. They don't act because they are symbols of freedom that oppose the Exarchs, and coercion is literally antithetical to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine their research into the Inferno must be acting on pure sunk cost fallacy at this point. <br /> <br /> You can't gain any meaningful information on it without shattering your sanity beyond recognition, can't treat with the entities safely and can't visit the realm. Any summoning rituals risk exposing reality to some of the worst horrors possible and all research material should have big, bold warnings in High Speech and Fallen languages saying &quot;<b>DO NOT POKE !</b>&quot;. <br /> <br /> In many ways its worse than researching the Abyss, because you can never make sense of the Void by definition. In the case of the Inferno, you don't want to know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-14-2022, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T13:30:12-07:00","id":1490175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Armsley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/585138-dark-eras-mage-selling-soul-to-the-devil?p=1490164#post1490164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, it's my personal headfanon that the Watchtowers *are* the Oracles, who made the ultimate sacrifice and performed the highest Imperial working possible to keep magic alive. They don't act because they are symbols of freedom that oppose the Exarchs, and coercion is literally antithetical to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is headcanon, as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T12:46:27-07:00","id":1490280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Armsley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/585138-dark-eras-mage-selling-soul-to-the-devil?p=1490164#post1490164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't act because they are symbols of freedom that oppose the Exarchs, and coercion is literally antithetical to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think I've heard that before. That's a pretty clever idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://foru